WEBVTT

00:02:27.609 --> 00:02:30.120
he wouldn't have been 14 feet behind,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.439
he would have been within one stride.

00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:34.181
Rather than the last beep,

00:02:34.181 --> 00:02:37.121
Owens would have been the second beep.

00:02:37.121 --> 00:02:39.172
Listen to it again.

00:02:39.172 --> 00:02:40.910
(Beeps)

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.293
That's the difference track
surface technology has made,

00:02:43.293 --> 00:02:45.572
and it's done it throughout the running world.

00:02:45.572 --> 00:02:47.303
Consider a longer event.

00:02:47.303 --> 00:02:50.266
In 1954, Sir Roger Bannister

00:02:50.266 --> 00:02:53.443
became the first man to run
under four minutes in the mile.

00:02:53.443 --> 00:02:56.493
Nowadays, college kids do that every year.

00:02:56.493 --> 00:02:59.046
On rare occasions, a high school kid does it.

00:02:59.046 --> 00:03:00.788
As of the end of last year,